---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Truth to Live By handles information across its website, contact route and owner-operated publishing system."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span>
      <h1>Privacy, considered.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Clear information about what this website does with your data.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-page">
      <aside class="sample-note">
        <strong>Prepared for owner and OAuth review.</strong> This notice remains part of the local
        website preview. The owner must approve it before public deployment or on-site email
        collection.
      </aside>
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Truth to Live By is operated by its owner in Ireland. Privacy questions, requests and
        concerns can be sent through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> to the dedicated Truth
        to Live By email address. The controller description and any further particulars required
        for public launch remain subject to owner review.
      </p>

      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>
        The website does not include a website contact form, advertising tracker or analytics
        service. Fonts and illustrations are served with the site. It does not use a database or
        create visitor accounts. On-site newsletter collection remains disabled in the preview.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site does not deliberately store cookies or local-storage identifiers. Ordinary hosting
        or local server request logs may record technical request information; the production
        hosting configuration and retention details have not yet been confirmed.
      </p>
      <h2>Links to other services</h2>
      <p>
        Links to YouTube, Instagram, TikTok, Facebook and the newsletter on beehiiv take you to
        those services. Their own privacy information applies when you visit them or choose to
        subscribe there. No YouTube player or beehiiv form is loaded automatically in this preview.
      </p>
      <h2>Playing videos</h2>
      <p>
        Pressing Play loads a YouTube privacy-enhanced player on this site and connects your browser
        to YouTube. YouTube can then receive technical and playback information and may use storage.
        Privacy-enhanced mode does not make playback anonymous. Before Play, thumbnails are served
        locally and no YouTube player connection is made. Closing a video removes its player.
      </p>
      <h2>Before on-site newsletter signup opens</h2>
      <p>
        The final notice must identify the site’s data controller and contact details, the selected
        newsletter service, the information collected, the relevant purposes and legal bases,
        retention arrangements, any international transfers and the safeguards that apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        It must also explain withdrawal of consent and the applicable rights to access, correction,
        erasure, restriction, objection and portability, along with how to exercise them and how to
        complain to the appropriate supervisory authority.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact correspondence</h2>
      <p>
        The Contact page opens your email application to write to the dedicated Truth to Live By
        Gmail address. The website does not receive or store the message itself. Google processes
        correspondence sent to that mailbox. Correspondence is used to respond to the enquiry,
        consider corrections or manage a requested professional relationship. Retention is limited
        to what is reasonably needed for those purposes and any applicable legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>The owner-operated publishing application</h2>
      <p>
        Truth to Live By uses a private publishing application to manage approved content for its
        official channels. The application is not a service offered to website visitors. Its Google
        OAuth connection is authorised by the channel owner and is used to confirm the intended
        YouTube channel, refresh the authorised session and upload owner-selected videos with their
        titles, descriptions and related metadata.
      </p>
      <p>
        For these operations, the application processes the authorised YouTube channel identifier
        and title; OAuth access and refresh credentials; locally selected video files and publishing
        metadata; and the video identifiers, status and operational responses returned by YouTube.
        It does not receive the owner’s Google password.
      </p>
      <p>
        Media and credentials remain in the owner-controlled local publishing environment. They are
        excluded from the website and source repositories. Publishing state and operational logs are
        kept separately for each brand. Google information is used only to provide the requested
        channel verification and upload functions. It is not sold, used for advertising or shared
        with unrelated third parties.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google and YouTube process information when the owner authorises the application and when
        the application checks a channel, refreshes authorisation or uploads a video. Their own
        terms and privacy information also apply. The owner can revoke access through the
        authorising Google Account’s security settings. Local OAuth credentials and publishing
        records can then be deleted from the publishing environment. See{' '}
        <a href="/publishing/">Publishing system</a>
        for a plain-language description of the application.
      </p>

      <h2>Rights and requests</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the circumstances, applicable data-protection rights may include access,
        correction, erasure, restriction, objection and portability, along with the right to
        complain to the appropriate supervisory authority. Use the{' '}
        <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> to make a request. Identity may need to be confirmed
        before a request is completed.
      </p>
      <h2>Future changes</h2>
      <p>
        Any introduction of analytics, embedded subscription forms or other processors requires a
        review of this notice and the actual data flows. A cookie-consent interface should be added
        only if the chosen implementation requires one.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the brand’s current contact route, see <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
